# Format and lint whatever is being committed, so nobody has to remember.
#
# lint-staged has been configured in package.json since the repo was set up, but
# this file never existed — and husky's dispatcher exits 0 when it is absent,
# silently. So nothing had ever run: 248 files had drifted out of Prettier's
# style by the time anyone noticed. CI checks both; this is what stops you
# finding out from a red build five minutes later.
#
# ESLint lives in each workspace, not at the root, with flat configs that
# resolve from the working directory — which is why a root-level `eslint` here
# would find no config and check nothing. `scripts/lint-staged-eslint.mjs`
# groups the staged files by the workspace that owns them and runs that
# workspace's own ESLint with that workspace as its cwd, so the hook and
# `pnpm turbo run lint` agree about what counts as an error.
#
# No `eslint --fix`: the hook reports, it does not rewrite code you are about to
# commit without showing you.
#
# --concurrent false because Prettier writes the same files ESLint then reads.
# In parallel, ESLint can read one mid-write — a parse error that depends on
# timing, which is the worst kind of failure to have in a commit hook.
lint-staged --concurrent false
